# Copy to .env (repo root) and fill in what you use — one file feeds every
# process: `npm run dev` (server/agent load it via dotenv, client via Vite's
# envDir) and Docker Compose (which injects it as real container env vars).
# Never commit the real .env.

# --- Supabase (required — see DEPLOY.md for project setup) ---
# SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@db.xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co:5432/postgres
# On a network that blocks outbound 5432, `npm run dev:db` runs a local
# embedded Postgres with the schema applied; use this instead:
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:55432/postgres
# Same URL/publishable key, exposed to the browser bundle (Vite requires the
# VITE_ prefix); values are identical to SUPABASE_URL/SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY above.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key

# --- Agent (optional — without a key the workspace runs with no AI agent) ---
# AGENT_PROVIDER=gemini            # "gemini" (default) or "claude"
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key   # gemini provider only
# AGENT_NAME=noodle
# AGENT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash     # or claude-sonnet-5 for the claude provider
# claude provider: no API key. Run `claude login` once on this host so the
# bundled claude CLI has a subscription session before starting the agent.
# CLAUDE_WORKDIR=./data/workspace  # cwd for Claude Code's native file/bash tools

# --- Login (unset both = clients see a "contact support" dead end) ---
# Google sign-in and email/password are both configured in the Supabase
# dashboard (Authentication → Providers); these two flags only control
# whether the client shows each option — they do not enable the provider.
# GOOGLE_AUTH_ENABLED=1
# EMAIL_AUTH=1
# Local test login (see AGENTS.md): test@test.com / testuser
# If email/password sign-in is enabled, decide whether Authentication → Settings →
# "Confirm email" should be on. This app's UI does not currently have a "check your
# email" step — leaving it off gives the same zero-friction signup the app had before
# this migration; turning it on will strand new signups on this app's UI until that
# flow is built.
# Long random secret the agent presents to join an auth-enabled server:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# AGENT_TOKEN=

# --- GitHub repositories (optional; set all five to enable Projects) ---
# A partial set (e.g. client id/secret without APP_ID/SLUG/PRIVATE_KEY) makes
# the server refuse to start. Comment all of them out for a no-GitHub stack.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=your-numeric-github-app-id
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=convyio
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your-github-app-client-id
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your-github-app-client-secret
# Paste the generated PEM private key; Railway accepts multiline values.
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"
# Optional fixed callback; otherwise the server derives /api/git/github/callback from its request origin.
# GITHUB_REDIRECT_URI=https://app.convyio.com/api/git/github/callback

# --- Server (container defaults are fine; see DEPLOY.md for the full table) ---
# PORT=3001
# DATA_DIR=/data   # workspace sandboxes and managed Git checkouts; the database
                    # and uploads live in Supabase.
